::  name       skate kind ceiling gate
::  shape      kind - int (@u32) -> lawful - int (@u32)
::  invariant  answers 1 while the input kind stays within the eight seated doors; answers 0 past the wall
::  example    3 -> 1 · 9 -> 0
::  readers    Skate · the native surface · Glow
::  nib        loca-skate-binding-v0 · the first Skate law spoken in Glow (20260829)
::
::  The event ring's domain seats eight input kinds -- key and mouse and touch,
::  down and up, moved and cancelled -- and Rye's own wall is max_kind = 8 in
::  brushstroke/skate_input_event.rye. This gate is that ceiling made runnable
::  in Glow itself; the witness proves the two spellings agree rather than
::  letting either drift alone. The floor (a kind of zero) is its sibling
::  gate's law, one conditional per desk as the lowerer speaks today.
|=  sample=@u32
?:  (gth sample 8)  0  1
